* Factorials. Each time round, f is multiplied by the next n.
1.1 Set f = f·n.
1.2 Type n, f in form 1.
Form 1:
__ factorial is _________
Set f = 1.
Do part 1 for n = 1(1)12.
 1 factorial is         1
 2 factorial is         2
 3 factorial is         6
 4 factorial is        24
 5 factorial is       120
 6 factorial is       720
 7 factorial is      5040
 8 factorial is     40320
 9 factorial is    362880
10 factorial is   3628800
11 factorial is  39916800
12 factorial is 479001600
* 13 factorial has ten digits. JOSS keeps nine, and says so by its notation.
Type 13·f.
    13·f =       6.2270208·10*9
